in @code
in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @nl
in @property

# @code/rust/macro — the Rust altitude's macro-reception sub-prism.
#
# The recognition (2026-06-08, Alex → Mara, T23, spec
# docs/specs/code-macro-surface.md): `@code/X.render` is the gap;
# `@code/X.macro` is the reception. T17 landed the render half at
# `@code/mirror.render` (the Wadler/Bernardy combinator surface, AST
# → text). This shard lands the Rust altitude's reception half: the
# language-side compile-time AST consumption layer that catches the
# substrate's emission via Rust's proc-macro surface
# (`#[proc_macro]`, `#[proc_macro_derive]`, `#[proc_macro_attribute]`).
#
# Why under `@code/rust` (not a new `@code/macro` family): per the
# spec's §2 substrate-pull check, `@code` is already the universal
# grammar-at-altitude discipline, and `@code/X` species already
# carry per-language altitude grammars. The macro sub-prism IS-A
# part of the language altitude (the way `@code/rust/cargo` IS-A
# part of `@code/rust`), not a sibling family. Path-namespace
# property per [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]: this
# file at `shards/code/rust/macro.mirror` declares
# `@code/rust/macro`. The path IS the declaration.
#
# === The smallest tick (this landing) ===
#
# Per the spec's §12 "Implementation cascade — the smallest tick
# that proves the shape":
#
#   - `shim_type(d: declaration) -> code/rust.ast { \ }` for the
#     simplest substrate-declaration kind (the `type` kind) end-to-
#     end through `prism/derive/src/declaration.rs`'s `declaration!`
#     proc-macro plus a round-trip OID test.
#   - The other three declaration kinds (`prism`, `action`,
#     `grammar`) are forward-promised here per the per-kind dispatch
#     in §10.1; their bodies are `\` until a consumer-pull tick
#     lands them.
#
# === Spec context ===
#
# docs/specs/code-macro-surface.md §4 (typed surface), §4.1 (four
# kinds dispatch), §5 (the four laws formalized), §6 (round-trip
# identity — the central contract), §10.1 (the dispatch table),
# §12 (the cascade).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]],
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
# Related shards: code.mirror (universal parent — declares the macro
# discipline at the family root), code/rust.mirror (the Rust altitude
# the sub-prism specialises), code/mirror.mirror (T17 — the render
# half at the mirror altitude; the sibling-altitude precedent for the
# round-trip law).

prism @code/rust/macro {
  focus macro
  project macro
  split macro
  shift macro
  settle macro
}

# === shim — the macro-emission contract ===
#
# Per spec §4: the macro shim's typed contract. Input is a substrate
# declaration `ref` (the `.mirror` declaration the macro is realising
# — typically a single `type` decl, or a `prism` decl, or an `action`
# decl with `\` body). Output is the language-altitude AST that, when
# expanded by the language's macro layer, produces the executable
# realisation of the substrate declaration. The body is `\` per
# consumer-pull discipline.
#
# This tick lands the `type` kind only (per §12); the other three
# kinds are forward-promised as their own sibling actions below with
# `\` bodies and the corresponding kind discriminator.

shim_type(d: declaration) -> code/rust.ast { \ }

# Forward-promised kinds (per spec §4.1 / §10.1 dispatch table).
# Each remains `\` until a consumer-pull tick. The cascade order
# per the brief is: type (this tick) → prism → action → grammar.

shim_prism(d: declaration) -> code/rust.ast { \ }
shim_action(d: declaration) -> code/rust.ast { \ }
shim_grammar(d: declaration) -> code/rust.ast { \ }

# === The four laws (per spec §5) ===
#
# Each law applies to every `shim_X` above. Declared here once at
# the sub-prism altitude; each action above inherits the obligation.
#
# 1. Type-soundness: for every declaration D, the emitted
#    `code/rust.ast` signature matches D's typed contract under
#    `@code/rust.type_mapping(D.args, D.ret)`. The substrate's typed
#    contract IS the Rust function's typed contract — the gap is
#    typed.
#
# 2. Round-trip identity: for every D,
#    `parse_rust(render_rust(shim_X(D))) = shim_X(D)` structurally.
#    The macro emission is a fixed point of the Rust-altitude parse
#    cycle — the gap closes deterministically. Same shape as the
#    `round_trip(render)` law declared on `@code/mirror.render` at
#    `shards/code/mirror.mirror` (T17, sibling altitude).
#
# 3. OID functionality: for substrate declarations D1, D2 with
#    `oid(D1) = oid(D2)`,
#    `oid(render_rust(shim_X(D1))) = oid(render_rust(shim_X(D2)))`.
#    The shim is a function of the substrate OID; same substrate
#    OID, same emitted OID — the gap is content-addressed.
#
# 4. Substrate-pull preservation: if D is substrate-realisable per
#    `@mirror/realisation.classify(D) = substrate(target)`, then
#    `shim_X(D)` references only Rust constructs that themselves
#    appear in some `@code/rust` substrate-realisable shard. The
#    emission cannot reach into `@io` to fill a substrate-realisable
#    gap. The discriminator's verdict IS the discriminator of the
#    shim — the gap respects the glass wall.

requires round_trip(shim_type)
requires oid_function(shim_type)
requires substrate_pull_preserving(shim_type)

requires round_trip(shim_prism)
requires oid_function(shim_prism)
requires substrate_pull_preserving(shim_prism)

requires round_trip(shim_action)
requires oid_function(shim_action)
requires substrate_pull_preserving(shim_action)

requires round_trip(shim_grammar)
requires oid_function(shim_grammar)
requires substrate_pull_preserving(shim_grammar)

out @code/rust/macro
out shim_type
out shim_prism
out shim_action
out shim_grammar
